course: dictionary
lesson: 8737
title: Serious words, serious meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: «Seriously» is an adverb, a word that tells us how something is done. It can mean in a serious way, not joking: «Take your homework seriously.» It can also mean very badly, as in «seriously hurt».
explain: Read the words around it to find which meaning fits. «Never throw anything from a balcony; even a small object falling from a height can seriously hurt someone below.» The word hurt tells you the meaning is very badly, so this is about real harm, not about being serious.
explain: Say «seriously?» with a surprised voice and you are asking, do you really mean that? Ask: what word would fit here? Then put your meaning into the sentence and check that it still makes sense.
explain: Schools and grown-ups use the phrase when they give warnings: «Mocking someone's religion, skin, body, family or food is bullying, and schools take it seriously.» Take seriously means treat it as important, not as a joke.
fact: Seriously can mean in a serious way, not joking.
fact: Seriously can mean very badly, as in «seriously ill» or «seriously injured».
fact: «Seriously?» is said when you are surprised or cannot believe something.
fact: Useful phrases include take seriously, seriously ill, seriously injured and seriously though.
fact: Seriously is the adverb form of the adjective serious, so it describes how an action is done.
exercise: «Take your homework seriously.» What does seriously mean here? | Happily | Very badly | Quickly and quietly | *In a serious way, not joking
exercise: «A small object falling from a height can seriously hurt someone below.» What does seriously mean here? | Slowly | Politely | Happily | *Very badly
exercise: Ben's friend says he has just won a prize. Ben replies, «Seriously?» What is Ben saying? | He is angry with his friend | He is tired and wants to sleep | *He is surprised and cannot believe it | He is joking
test: «Schools take bullying seriously.» What does take seriously mean? | *Treat it as important, not as a joke | Ignore it and laugh | Write it on a list | Forget it by lunchtime
test: The doctor said Sam was seriously ill, so he stayed in bed. What does seriously mean here? | Quietly | In a serious way, not joking | Happily | *Very badly
exam: Which sentence uses seriously to mean very badly? | *«The fall seriously injured the climber.» | «The kite flew away quickly.» | «Seriously?» he said, and laughed | «Please take your reading seriously.»
